      "problem": "If a square has a side length of $30\\,\\text{ft},$ what is its area?",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(30\\,\\text{ft})^{2} \\\\  & =30\\,\\text{ft}\\times 30\\,\\text{ft} \\\\  & =(30\\times 30)\\times (\\text{ft}\\times \\text{ft}) \\\\  & =900\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
